 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation: fà, Guglielmo's “di riso di, riso” (bars 40–41, the comma as printed), and “si troverà” (bars 80–84, not in the libretto; taken as “it will be found”). Don Alfonso's “belba” in bar 61 is a print slip: it keeps the printed letters with the IPA and meaning of bella (ˈbɛl.la). All six sing the same words; each singer has his or her own phrases. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L65, IPA checked against Castel), repeated where the score repeats the text; repeated fragments have short literal translations. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
